ield/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc06c13a-02a5-52da-8c5f-33478dd82019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439743} {:answer/id #uuid "0477e31a-6a45-5821-ab82-2a1844d48dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc06c13a-02a5-52da-8c5f-33478dd82019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439743} :answer-field/id #uuid "f85e3c8e-67f8-5920-9a7f-eec1efb5cb19" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2f92ee8b-33fa-5343-9c16-73df2f465b76" :question/math-academy-id "q-39934" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+8x}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-7$\n- **II.** $x=-2$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+8x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x+3)}{x({x}^{2}+2x+8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}(x+3)}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2x+8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3}{{x}^{2}+2x+8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2x+8=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-4(1)(8) \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31eacf5a-75a5-5b38-8c24-4b1598ecf3a7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points of Discontinuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c38f2c4-b53b-5536-b039-2a4124135cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439819} {:answer/id #uuid "998e2a28-c47b-5148-a261-c01e0ac02633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c38f2c4-b53b-5536-b039-2a4124135cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439819} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3237d3d-febe-5bac-8a8b-854e66228e33" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e5ab529-8814-5641-9c16-a8010dc0d41f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439821} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc129f9-2e75-52bc-b78c-3799d4b6c7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc129f9-2e75-52bc-b78c-3799d4b6c7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439822} :answer-field/id #uuid "9375134b-1c01-5cfd-9a5f-168dfb7500a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ide