ype/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d87d550-5004-5d22-b9a3-b2335e96082d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6913" :question/problem "Find all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-2$\n- **II.** $x=- \\sqrt{2}$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=\\sqrt{2}$\n- **V.** $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ does not have any vertical asymptotes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46af019b-5e0e-54fe-a3a4-d3a5f79204d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440035} {:answer/id #uuid "36089e95-fc88-5a76-b2c4-311f215a41a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46af019b-5e0e-54fe-a3a4-d3a5f79204d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440035} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7bba9ed-822d-53ee-89c9-116fde41ee52" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "242f0892-e1e1-5e47-ac02-f10209cc7691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440037} {:answer/id #uuid "5261eeed-b902-50cd-be8c-e339e0cd7603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5261eeed-b902-50cd-be8c-e339e0cd7603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440038} :answer-field/id #uuid "3baa83a4-cb6e-5db3-8f0f-7d1c5b2abfae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8201e6-2d8f-5889-8d5a-7f26e45965c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440039} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa3b90b-7a80-5418-b7a0-778bc241d10d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aa3b90b-7a80-5418-b7a0-778bc241d10d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440040} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab487ccf-fee0-51d3-aff0-dfee470b09fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11af43ea-89bf-58ea-b458-4433226aa764" :question/math-academy-id "q-9913" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix  $[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}]$ is singular.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $k=-2$\n- **II.** $k=0$\n- **III.** $k=2$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}| & =k|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(3k-6)+0+0 \\\\  & =k(3k-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(3k-6) & =0 \\\\ 3k(k-2) & =0 \\\\ k & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=0$ and $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31eacf5a-75a5-5b38-8c24-4b1598ecf3a7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points of Discontinuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e60b367-e517-57db-8d1a-b1fef0a9dffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439385} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2bd2ff-ef0f-54af-8e8c-3db63c8766d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e60b367-e517-57db-8d1a-b1fef0a9dffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439385} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a438c3b-98c9-5c64-9d05-c001bc1efd71" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/i